            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MUSIC_MINX"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Consider dry-frying the cumin seeds in a cast iron frying pan for several minutes before adding to the rice. When you hear them \"pop\" they are ready. Heat the peas before adding to rice."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "greenmonkey8"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent, excellent recipe. I didn't have cumin seeds, so I used a 1/2 teaspoon of cumin powder. I also used chicken broth in place of the water. It was the most delicious and savory rice I've ever had!! I served it with chicken and veggie kabobs. It turned out well, like a restaurant dish! Thank you for this recipe!!",
            "datePublished": "2009-08-21T05:40:38.703Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "France C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Next time I'll just use my usual method (water/rice ratio &amp; cook time) for the rice, as it came out super mushy. As others have mentioned this also needs salt and the cumin seeds would be more flavorful if toasted beforehand. Given these tweaks, it could be a 5 star recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2020-09-23T23:14:18.663Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Foody"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Decent basmati rice. I made this using brown basmati. After presoaking the rice for half an hour, and straining it, I added the water. 3/4 tsp ground cumin, 1/2 tsp salt, and a half Tbsp of vegetable oil. After the rice cooked, I fluffed it and stirred in the hot, cooked peas. Great with curry!",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-10T01:26:14.437Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Denise B"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a really tasty and fast rice dish! I rinsed the rice in cold water first, and then cooked it in chicken broth with 1 tablespoon of margarine in the microwave (the easiest way to cook rice perfectly.) I didn't have any cumin seed so I used 1/2 teaspoon of ground cumin. I also added a little turmeric for color and flavor and garam masala to intensify the Indian flavor. This recipe was so simple and went great with my garlic and herb chicken breasts. I will definitely make this again!",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-06T18:22:35.767Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ManganTayun"
            },
            "reviewBody": "For a quick, fried cumin addition (as is suggested by a reviewer), I fry the cumin in the pot before adding the rice and water. And like many suggested, do add salt! Saffron or turmeric may also be added with the rice for a nice color and flavor.",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-14T13:04:52.077Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LCURT"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow how easy can it get?! I made the rice in my rice cooker as usual and then added the cumin seeds (not ground) and frozen peas when it was done. Closed the lid and let it mesh together for a few minutes and the peas were cooked and rice flavorful.",
            "datePublished": "2006-09-29T18:13:33.513Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Clarigon"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is spot-on. My only change was to omit the cumin and add a heaping teaspoon of sweet curry powder to the water. The curry added a nice boost of both flavor and color. With or without curry (or cumin), this recipe is a keeper!",
            "datePublished": "2016-09-12T21:15:14.753Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tracey Ferrari Posner"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made by toasting the cumin seeds, added 1 cinnamon stick and a few anise seeds from another reviewer's suggestion then proceeded with the recipe. Next time, I will do the same thing except I will use a whole star anise pod instead of the seeds for a a bit more flavor.",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-30T02:54:33.867Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Leah"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I find that it helps to soak the rice in a bowl of water first. Also, when cooking the rice (I usually just use my rice cooker), I like to add a cinnamon stick, 2 cloves, and a couple anise seeds to give it a more traditional flavor and great aroma!",
            "datePublished": "2007-12-05T12:07:43.857Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TheKnittingJedi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I served this rice with a chickpea curry and it was the perfect addition. I cooked the rice with veggie broth instead of water to give it some more flavor, and I used 1/2 tsp of ground cumin which was all I had on hand. Easy and delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2013-01-16T19:57:40.410Z"
          },
